<rml>
<head>
	<title>Menu cursor</title>
	<link type="text/rcss" href="style/base.rcss"/>
</head>
<!--
	The drawn cursor for the game's own menus. While the pointer owns the
	mouse, relative mouse mode stays on and the OS cursor is hidden, so this
	document is the only thing on screen showing where the pointer is.
	src/runtime/ui/ui_menu_cursor.cpp shows and hides it and refreshes the
	model at the field boundary.

	The whole document is pointer-events: none: the mouse buttons belong to
	guest/menu_nav.cpp while the pointer has them, and an element that
	swallowed a click would take it from the game's menu.

	.cursor-area is placed on the presented scanout rectangle in percent of
	the surface, the same space guest/menu_nav.cpp hit-tests in, so the
	cursor lands where the hit test happens. .cursor-point inside it is a
	zero-sized box at the cursor position, so both cursors below place
	themselves in offsets from that one point.

	Two cursors, one shown at a time. The first is the letter I of the game's
	own wordmark, cut out of the title image built from the disc, turned to a
	mouse cursor's angle and outlined (src/runtime/ui/cursor_image.cpp). It is
	served from memory under the "cursor:" scheme, and it is offset by minus
	its hotspot so the glyph's point lands on the cursor position. The second,
	shown whenever no image could be built, is two triangles drawn out of
	borders (see base.rcss): a dark outer one with a lighter inner one over
	it. Both have their sharp corner at their own top left, which is the point
	.cursor-point sits on, so the tip is on the cursor either way.
-->
<body class="cursor-body" data-model="menucursor">
	<div class="cursor-area"
	     data-style-left="present_left" data-style-top="present_top"
	     data-style-width="present_width" data-style-height="present_height">
		<div class="cursor-point"
		     data-style-left="cursor_left" data-style-top="cursor_top">
			<img class="menu-cursor-image" data-if="image_cursor"
			     data-attr-src="cursor_src"
			     data-style-left="image_left" data-style-top="image_top"
			     data-style-width="image_width" data-style-height="image_height"/>
			<div class="menu-cursor" data-if="!image_cursor">
				<div class="menu-cursor-fill"></div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
